// CORP FUNKHY 2 — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CORP FUNKHY 2 — Peter's CORP FUNKHY (corp-funkhy, his desk copy of CORPORATE KOMBAT — BLUE
// CHIP) with four new riff lanes, made from it on 24 Oct 2026. Everything of his — bank, mix,
// arrangement, groups, mutes, levels — is as he had it; GROUP 1 (the MOOG call, the DX bell, the
// HORNS answer) stays muted. A desk copy: the game does not play this file.
// 
// Peter: "create a new track that contains the notes from all of these combined into one… follow
// the groove of the bassline… notes dropping out so it's not so busy and the bassline gets to
// drive… 4 different tracks with variants on the combined main riff".
// 
// The riff: GROUP 1's three lanes merged bar by bar as they play (in the first half of a bar the
// call's note wins a shared onset, in the second the answer's), every note moved onto the bass's
// own onsets (a sixteenth at most, earlier first) or dropped, each ending by the next bass note,
// then thinned to keep the downbeats, the bar's first note and the phrase ends. In GROUP 2:
//   lead6  RIFF A · Rhodes (sparse) — rmndTineEP, 96 of 214 (45%) of the combined notes, two sixteenths apart at least — ON
//   lead7  RIFF B · Nylon (medium) — frppNylon, 147 of 214 (69%) — muted
//   lead8  RIFF C · Vibes dyads (strong beats) — mrdrVibraphone, 53 of 214 (25%), each with a chord tone under it — muted
//   lead9  RIFF D · Kalimba (call, 8va) — frppKalimba, the MOOG call alone an octave up, 84 of 214 (39%) — muted
// Unmute one at a time on the desk to compare. Written by work/local/_corp-funkhy-2.mjs, which reads
// corp-funkhy.js fresh each run; it refuses to overwrite this file once the desk has saved it.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
